WEBVTT

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.860
[Lightning] How great would it have been
to see this place in its heyday!

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.740
Oh, I can't tell you how many times
I've dreamed of that.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.420
But one of these days we'll
find a way to get it back on the map.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.180
Yeah. Hey, listen, thanks for the drive.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.100
I had a great time.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.900
It's kinda nice to slow down
every once in a while.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.700
You're welcome.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.340
Hey, listen, listen!

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.500
If anybody asks you,
we was out smashin' mailboxes, OK?

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.660
[chuckling] Wha... what?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.980
[rumbling]

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.700
[mooing]

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.060
Oh, man, the paint's still wet!

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.700
- [honking loudly]
- [mooing]

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.540
No, no, no, no!
Get out of the store!

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.220
Hey! Don't eat the radial!
Here, take-a the snow tires.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.580
- [Sheriff] Mater!
- I wasn't tractor-tippin'!

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.660
Then where did all these
gol-durn tractors come from?

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.260
- Whoa, boy!
- Hey! Hey, guys!

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.300
There's one goin' this way.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.460
I got it.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.260
Come here, little tractor,
come here.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.620
Yeah, that's a good tractor.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.020
No, no, no, no, come here.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.460
What are you doing?

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:20.220
You're not supposed to go
wandering off all...

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.900
...alone.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.540
What are you doin'
with those old racin' tires?

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.540
[sighing heavily]

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.500
Come on, Doc, drive.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.380
[revs engine]

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.180
Ah... Yeah.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:07.940
- Wow.
- Huh?

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.580
You're amazing!

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.820
[coughing] What are you doin'?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.620
Doc, wait!

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.380
[trucks mooing]

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.900
Giddup right in there!
Come on, Rusty.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.980
Doc, hold it!
Seriously, your driving's incredible!

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.380
- Wonderful. Now, go away.
- Hey, I mean it. You've still got it!

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.300
- I'm askin' you to leave.
- Come on.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.340
I'm a racecar,
you're a much older racecar,

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.420
but under the hood
you and I are the same.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.540
We are not the same!
Understand? Now, get out.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.540
How could a car like you quit
at the top of your game?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.900
You think I quit?

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.180
[Lightning] Right.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.420
Your big wreck in '54.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.500
They quit on me.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.100
When I finally got put together,
I went back expecting a big welcome.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.060
You know what they said?
"You're history."

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:19.220
Moved right on to
the next rookie standing in line.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.300
There was a lot left in me.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:28.060
I never got a chance to show 'em.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.540
I keep that to remind me
never to go back.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.900
I just never expected that
that world would...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.180
...would find me here.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.900
- Hey, look, Doc, I'm not them.
- Oh, yeah?

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:44.940
No, I'm not.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:48.860
When is the last time you cared about
something except yourself, hot rod?

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:53.540
You name me one time
and I will take it all back.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.380
Uh-huh. I didn't think so.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.540
These are good folk around here,
who care about one another.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.300
I don't want 'em depending
on someone they can't count on.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:08.900
Oh, like you?
You've been here how long

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.220
and your friends
don't even know who you are?

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.940
Who's caring about only himself?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.820
Just finish that road
and get outta here!

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.820
[reveille plays]

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.900
[♪ Jimi Hendrix: Star Spangled Banner]

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:33.660
[Sarge] Will you turn that
disrespectful junk off?

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.140
[Fillmore] Respect the classics, man.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.220
[snoring]

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.380
[snorts, putters]

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.820
[grunting]

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.700
[smacking] Ah...

